The two files connect through one file called **questions-bank.json**. You make it with the first file and your students read it with the second.

**The idea**
1. **pdf-to-mcq.html** is for you only (the admin). You upload a PDF and it makes the questions.
2. It gives you a file called **questions-bank.json**, which holds all your approved questions.
3. **quiz.html** is for your students. When it opens, it automatically reads questions-bank.json from the same folder and makes the quiz.

So the quiz page never touches the PDF. It only reads the JSON file.

**Step by step**

*On your own computer (once per PDF):*
1. Open `pdf-to-mcq.html` in Chrome. You need internet for this step, because the PDF reader and OCR load online.
2. Fill in the source name, exam, subject and year. Tick the box that says you are allowed to use this material.
3. Choose the PDF and click **Extract questions**. Wait until the questions appear.
4. Check each question. Fix mistakes, choose the correct answer and tick **Approve**.
5. Click **Publish approved questions**, then **Download questions-bank.json**.
6. To add more PDFs later, use "Existing questions-bank.json" to load your old file first. Your new questions are then added to it, and the downloaded file has everything.

*On your website:*
1. Upload **quiz.html** and **questions-bank.json** to the **same folder** on your hosting.
2. Make sure the file names are exactly `quiz.html` and `questions-bank.json`, in small letters.
3. Add a button on your home page:
   `<a href="quiz.html" class="quiz-btn">Start Quiz</a>`
4. Open `yourwebsite.com/quiz.html` to test. The subject buttons appear from your questions. Each time a student presses Start, they get a random set.

**Whenever you want to add new questions**
Do the first part again on your computer, then upload the new `questions-bank.json` to your website. It replaces the old one.

**Things to remember**
- Keep **pdf-to-mcq.html** on your own computer. Don't upload it to your public website, because anyone could open it.
- Upload only questions you are allowed to publish, such as official papers.
- Opening quiz.html by double-clicking it on your computer may not load the questions, because browsers block reading files that way. It works properly once the files are on the website. To test on your computer, open quiz.html and use the "Load a file" box to pick questions-bank.json.

